  "text": "### 6.2 Finding Classification  \n**Finding Severity:**  \n| Grade | Definition | Timeframe | Example |\n|-------|-----------|-----------|---------|\n| Critical | Control failure causing financial loss/regulatory breach | Remediate within 30 days | KYC not completed on account |\n| High | Control weakness with significant risk | Remediate within 90 days | Missing approvals on transactions |\n| Medium | Control gap with moderate impact | Remediate within 180 days | Process manual (could automate) |\n| Low | Control improvement opportunity | Remediate within 1 year | Outdated procedure, minor risk |  \n**Remediation Tracking:**\n- Management submits action plan (target date, responsible party)\n- Board Audit Committee reviews quarterly\n- Internal Audit follows up (re-test controls)\n- Closure when remediation verified  \n---",
